{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a new customizable Shopify theme section called “Split Conversion Hero”.
    
    Purpose:
    This section will be used for landing pages that promote downloadable resources, checklists, assessments, guides, and demo-related offers. It should feel clean, premium, calm, and conversion-focused. The design should work well for a B2B retail analytics / retail intelligence company.
    
    Layout:
    Create a responsive two-column hero section with one text column and one image column.
    
    The merchant should be able to choose whether the image appears on the left or the right on desktop.
    
    On mobile, the section should stack cleanly. Add a setting to choose mobile order:
    
    * Text first
    * Image first
    
    Text column fields:
    Include customizable fields for:
    
    * Eyebrow text
    * Heading
    * Rich text description
    * Optional bullet list with up to 4 bullet items
    * Primary button label
    * Primary button link
    * Optional secondary button label
    * Optional secondary button link
    * Small caption / reassurance text below the button area
    
    Text column behavior:
    The heading should be large and clear.
    The description should support rich text.
    The bullet list should be optional. If no bullet items are entered, the bullet list should not display.
    The secondary button should only display if both the label and link are entered.
    The caption should only display if text is entered.
    
    Image column fields:
    Include:
    
    * Image picker
    * Image alt text
    * Image position control: left or right on desktop
    * Image aspect ratio options:
    
      * Natural
      * 4:3
      * 3:2
      * 1:1
      * Portrait
    * Image fit options:
    
      * Cover
      * Contain
    * Image border radius control
    * Image shadow on/off
    * Image border on/off
    * Optional image background panel on/off
    
    Optional trust strip:
    Add an optional small trust strip below the hero copy or below the buttons. It should support up to 4 short text items, such as:
    
    * Free PDF
    * For retail teams
    * 5-minute checklist
    * No obligation
    
    If no trust strip items are entered, this area should not display.
    
    Section style controls:
    Include settings for:
    
    * Section background color
    * Text color
    * Heading color
    * Eyebrow color
    * Accent color
    * Button background color
    * Button text color
    * Secondary button color
    * Image panel background color
    * Maximum section width
    * Top padding
    * Bottom padding
    * Column gap
    * Desktop column width:
    
      * 50/50
      * 55/45 text/image
      * 45/55 text/image
    * Vertical alignment:
    
      * Top
      * Center
    
    Design direction:
    The section should feel like a polished B2B SaaS landing page, not an ecommerce product section.
    Use generous spacing, clean typography, soft rounded corners, restrained shadows, and clear hierarchy.
    Avoid visual clutter.
    Avoid decorative overlays that make text harder to read.
    The image should feel intentionally placed inside the layout, not like a heavy full-width banner.
    The CTA area should be clear and easy to scan.
    
    Responsive behavior:
    On desktop, display the two columns side by side.
    On tablet and mobile, stack the columns with comfortable spacing.
    Buttons should stack or wrap naturally on small screens.
    Image should scale cleanly without cropping important content.
    Text should remain readable and not become cramped.
    
    Accessibility:
    Use semantic HTML where possible.
    Ensure buttons are accessible links.
    Use the image alt text field.
    Maintain readable contrast between text and background.
    Do not display empty elements when optional fields are blank.
    
    Default content:
    Eyebrow: Free Retail Checklist
    Heading: Find the store execution gaps that are costing you sales
    Description: Use this checklist to review how your stores measure traffic, understand conversion, and turn operational data into action.
    Bullet 1: Review traffic and conversion visibility
    Bullet 2: Identify missed operational signals
    Bullet 3: Align store teams around clearer daily actions
    Primary button: Download the checklist
    Caption: Free resource for retail leaders, store operations teams, and DX managers.
    Trust item 1: Free PDF
    Trust item 2: Retail operations focused
    Trust item 3: Practical checklist
    Trust item 4: No obligation
    , Please refine the “Split Conversion Hero” section based on the following structural and visual requirements.
    
    Do not change the core two-column structure. Keep the text column and image column side by side on desktop, with mobile stacking.
    
    Primary refinements:
    
    1. Improve the left-column hierarchy
       The left text area should feel more polished and conversion-focused.
    
    Use this hierarchy:
    
    * Eyebrow
    * Heading
    * Description
    * Bullet list
    * CTA button row
    * Caption / reassurance text
    * Optional trust strip
    
    The spacing between these elements should feel intentional and balanced. Avoid large gaps between the button, caption, and trust strip.
    
    2. Eyebrow styling
       Make the eyebrow small, uppercase, and slightly letter-spaced.
       It should use the accent color.
       It should not feel too far away from the heading.
       Recommended styling:
    
    * Font size: 12–14px
    * Font weight: 600 or 700
    * Letter spacing: 0.06em to 0.1em
    * Margin-bottom: 18–24px
    
    3. Heading styling
       The heading should be large, strong, and readable.
       It should support line breaks naturally without feeling oversized.
       Recommended desktop styling:
    
    * Font size: 48–60px depending on screen width
    * Line height: 1.08–1.15
    * Font weight: 700 or 800
    * Max width: approximately 600px
    
    Recommended mobile styling:
    
    * Font size: 34–42px
    * Line height: 1.12–1.18
    
    4. Description styling
       The description should sit clearly below the heading and feel easy to read.
       Recommended styling:
    
    * Font size: 18–21px on desktop
    * Line height: 1.55–1.7
    * Max width: approximately 600px
    * Muted text color option
    * Margin-top: 22–28px
    
    5. Bullet list styling
       The bullet list should feel clean and premium, not like a default browser list.
    
    Requirements:
    
    * Use checkmark icons or simple accent marks
    * Allow the checkmark color to use the accent color
    * Remove default list indentation
    * Keep spacing between bullet items comfortable
    * Bullet text should align cleanly
    * Bullet list should have moderate spacing from the description and CTA
    
    Recommended styling:
    
    * Font size: 16–18px
    * Line height: 1.45–1.6
    * Gap between bullet items: 12–16px
    * Margin-top: 26–34px
    
    6. CTA button area
       The primary button should be visually clear and strong.
       The optional secondary button should sit beside it on desktop and stack naturally on mobile.
    
    Requirements:
    
    * Add a setting for button size: small / medium / large
    * Add a setting for button border radius
    * Add a setting for button alignment: left / center
    * Keep default alignment left on desktop
    * Button should not stretch full-width on desktop
    * On mobile, allow full-width button option
    
    Recommended default:
    
    * Medium-large button
    * Padding: 16px 26px
    * Border radius: 6–10px
    * Font weight: 600 or 700
    * Margin-top after bullets: 28–36px
    
    7. Caption / reassurance text
       The caption should sit close to the button, not feel disconnected.
       It should be smaller and quieter than the body text.
    
    Recommended styling:
    
    * Font size: 14–15px
    * Line height: 1.5
    * Muted color
    * Margin-top: 14–18px
    * Max width: approximately 560px
    
    8. Trust strip layout
       The trust strip should feel like a compact supporting row, not a separate section.
    
    Requirements:
    
    * Display trust items in one clean row on desktop when space allows
    * Wrap cleanly on smaller screens
    * Use small checkmarks or simple separators
    * Keep the trust strip visually lighter than the main bullet list
    * Add settings to control whether trust strip appears below the caption or below the full hero
    
    Recommended styling:
    
    * Font size: 14–15px
    * Gap between items: 18–28px
    * Margin-top: 22–28px
    * Muted color
    * Checkmark uses accent color
    
    9. Column alignment
       Add or refine vertical alignment controls:
    
    * Top
    * Center
    * Bottom
    
    Default should be center alignment on desktop so the image and text feel balanced.
    
    10. Section spacing
        The section should have generous but not excessive vertical spacing.
    
    Recommended default:
    
    * Desktop top padding: 80–110px
    * Desktop bottom padding: 80–110px
    * Mobile top padding: 56–72px
    * Mobile bottom padding: 56–72px
    
    11. Column width and gap
        Keep the existing desktop column width options, but make sure the text column does not become too narrow.
    
    Recommended defaults:
    
    * Desktop layout: 50/50 or 55/45 text/image
    * Column gap: 56–80px
    * Max section width: 1200–1320px
    
    12. Mobile refinements
        On mobile:
    
    * Text should not feel cramped
    * Heading should scale down cleanly
    * Bullet list should remain readable
    * CTA button should have an option to become full width
    * Trust strip should wrap into two rows if needed
    * Maintain clear spacing between image and text
    
    13. Avoid
        Do not add decorative effects that make the section feel busy.
        Do not add floating UI elements.
        Do not add background patterns unless optional and disabled by default.
        Do not center-align the entire text block by default.
        Do not make the trust strip too prominent.
        Do not display empty optional fields.
    
    Overall design direction:
    The left side should feel like , Please make a final refinement pass on the Split Conversion Hero section. Keep the existing two-column structure and do not change the feature set.
    
    The priority is to add stronger customization controls for typography, spacing, and CTA layout so the section can be adjusted visually inside the Shopify theme editor.
    
    Add the following controls:
    
    1. Heading controls
       Add settings to control:
    
    * Heading desktop font size
    * Heading mobile font size
    * Heading line height
    * Heading max width
    * Heading font weight
    * Heading color
    
    Use sensible default values, but make these adjustable in the theme editor.
    
    2. Eyebrow controls
       Add settings to control:
    
    * Eyebrow font size
    * Eyebrow letter spacing
    * Eyebrow font weight
    * Eyebrow color
    * Eyebrow bottom spacing
    
    3. Description controls
       Add settings to control:
    
    * Description font size
    * Description line height
    * Description max width
    * Description color
    * Description top spacing
    * Description bottom spacing
    
    4. Bullet list controls
       Add settings to control:
    
    * Bullet text font size
    * Bullet text line height
    * Bullet item spacing
    * Bullet list top spacing
    * Bullet list bottom spacing
    * Checkmark color
    * Checkmark size
    * Bullet text color
    
    The bullet list should remain clean and premium. Do not use default browser list styling.
    
    5. Button controls
       Add settings to control:
    
    * Primary button background color
    * Primary button text color
    * Primary button hover background color
    * Primary button hover text color
    * Button font size
    * Button font weight
    * Button border radius
    * Button vertical padding
    * Button horizontal padding
    * Button top spacing
    * Button alignment: left or center
    * Mobile button width: auto or full width
    
    If the secondary button is used, add equivalent color and border controls where appropriate.
    
    6. Caption controls
       Add settings to control:
    
    * Caption font size
    * Caption line height
    * Caption color
    * Caption max width
    * Caption top spacing
    * Caption bottom spacing
    
    The caption should sit visually close to the button by default.
    
    7. Trust strip controls
       Add settings to control:
    
    * Trust strip font size
    * Trust strip text color
    * Trust strip checkmark color
    * Trust strip item gap
    * Trust strip row gap
    * Trust strip top spacing
    * Trust strip alignment: left or center
    
    The trust strip should wrap cleanly and must never be cut off at the bottom of the section.
    
    8. Section spacing controls
       Add settings to control:
    
    * Desktop top padding
    * Desktop bottom padding
    * Mobile top padding
    * Mobile bottom padding
    * Column gap
    * Maximum section width
    
    Make sure the trust strip remains visible when section padding is adjusted.
    
    9. Column controls
       Keep or add controls for:
    
    * Image position on desktop: left or right
    * Desktop column ratio:
    
      * 50/50
      * 55/45 text/image
      * 45/55 text/image
      * 60/40 text/image
      * 40/60 text/image
    * Vertical alignment:
    
      * Top
      * Center
      * Bottom
    
    10. Mobile controls
        Add or keep controls for:
    
    * Mobile order: text first or image first
    * Mobile text alignment: left or center
    * Mobile button width: auto or full width
    * Mobile column spacing
    
    11. Visual behavior
        Do not add new decorative design elements.
        Do not add floating UI elements.
        Do not add background patterns.
        Do not center-align the entire section by default.
        Do not display empty optional fields.
    
    Default design direction:
    The section should default to a calm, premium B2B landing page look with strong hierarchy, generous spacing, and clear CTA visibility. The merchant should be able to fine-tune text size, spacing, and button proportions from the theme editor without editing code.
    
{% enddoc %}
{% assign ai_gen_id = block.id | replace: '_', '' | downcase %}

{% style %}
  .ai-split-hero-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: block;
    background-color: {{ block.settings.section_background }};
    padding-top: {{ block.settings.padding_top_mobile }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ block.settings.padding_bottom_mobile }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-split-hero-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding-top: {{ block.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ block.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-container-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-width: {{ block.settings.max_width }}px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-left: 24px;
    padding-right: 24px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-split-hero-container-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding-left: 40px;
      padding-right: 40px;
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: {{ block.settings.mobile_column_gap }}px;
    align-items: {{ block.settings.vertical_alignment }};
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-split-hero-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      gap: {{ block.settings.column_gap }}px;
      {% if block.settings.column_ratio == '50-50' %}
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      {% elsif block.settings.column_ratio == '55-45' %}
        grid-template-columns: 1.22fr 1fr;
      {% elsif block.settings.column_ratio == '45-55' %}
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.22fr;
      {% elsif block.settings.column_ratio == '60-40' %}
        grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr;
      {% elsif block.settings.column_ratio == '40-60' %}
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr;
      {% endif %}
    }

    .ai-split-hero-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }}--image-left {
      direction: rtl;
    }

    .ai-split-hero-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }}--image-left > * {
      direction: ltr;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ai-split-hero-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }}--text-first .ai-split-hero-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      order: 1;
    }

    .ai-split-hero-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }}--text-first .ai-split-hero-image-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      order: 2;
    }

    .ai-split-hero-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }}--image-first .ai-split-hero-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      order: 2;
    }

    .ai-split-hero-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }}--image-first .ai-split-hero-image-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      order: 1;
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    {% if block.settings.mobile_text_alignment == 'center' %}
      text-align: center;
    {% endif %}
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-split-hero-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      text-align: left;
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-eyebrow-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.eyebrow_font_size }}px;
    font-weight: {{ block.settings.eyebrow_font_weight }};
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: {{ block.settings.eyebrow_letter_spacing }}em;
    color: {{ block.settings.eyebrow_color }};
    margin: 0 0 {{ block.settings.eyebrow_bottom_spacing }}px 0;
  }

  .ai-split-hero-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.heading_font_size_mobile }}px;
    line-height: {{ block.settings.heading_line_height }};
    font-weight: {{ block.settings.heading_font_weight }};
    color: {{ block.settings.heading_color }};
    margin: 0;
    max-width: {{ block.settings.heading_max_width }}px;
    {% if block.settings.mobile_text_alignment == 'center' %}
      margin-left: auto;
      margin-right: auto;
    {% endif %}
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-split-hero-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.heading_font_size }}px;
      margin-left: 0;
      margin-right: 0;
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.description_font_size }}px;
    line-height: {{ block.settings.description_line_height }};
    color: {{ block.settings.description_color }};
    margin-top: {{ block.settings.description_top_spacing }}px;
    margin-bottom: {{ block.settings.description_bottom_spacing }}px;
    max-width: {{ block.settings.description_max_width }}px;
    {% if block.settings.mobile_text_alignment == 'center' %}
      margin-left: auto;
      margin-right: auto;
    {% endif %}
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-split-hero-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      margin-left: 0;
      margin-right: 0;
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} p {
    margin: 0 0 16px 0;
  }

  .ai-split-hero-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .ai-split-hero-bullets-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: {{ block.settings.bullet_list_top_spacing }}px 0 {{ block.settings.bullet_list_bottom_spacing }}px 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: {{ block.settings.bullet_item_spacing }}px;
    {% if block.settings.mobile_text_alignment == 'center' %}
      align-items: center;
    {% endif %}
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-split-hero-bullets-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-bullet-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 12px;
    font-size: {{ block.settings.bullet_font_size }}px;
    line-height: {{ block.settings.bullet_line_height }};
    color: {{ block.settings.bullet_text_color }};
  }

  .ai-split-hero-bullet-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: {{ block.settings.checkmark_size }}px;
    height: {{ block.settings.checkmark_size }}px;
    margin-top: 2px;
    color: {{ block.settings.checkmark_color }};
  }

  .ai-split-hero-cta-wrapper-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    margin-top: {{ block.settings.button_top_spacing }}px;
  }

  .ai-split-hero-buttons-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: center;
    {% if block.settings.button_alignment == 'center' %}
      justify-content: center;
    {% else %}
      justify-content: flex-start;
    {% endif %}
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ai-split-hero-buttons-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      {% if block.settings.mobile_text_alignment == 'center' %}
        justify-content: center;
      {% endif %}
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-button-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: {{ block.settings.button_font_weight }};
    font-size: {{ block.settings.button_font_size }}px;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: {{ block.settings.button_border_radius }}px;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    padding: {{ block.settings.button_vertical_padding }}px {{ block.settings.button_horizontal_padding }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ai-split-hero-button-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      {% if block.settings.mobile_button_width == 'full' %}
        width: 100%;
      {% endif %}
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-button-primary-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    background-color: {{ block.settings.primary_button_background }};
    color: {{ block.settings.primary_button_text }};
  }

  .ai-split-hero-button-primary-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover {
    background-color: {{ block.settings.primary_button_hover_background }};
    color: {{ block.settings.primary_button_hover_text }};
  }

  .ai-split-hero-button-secondary-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    background-color: {{ block.settings.secondary_button_background }};
    color: {{ block.settings.secondary_button_text }};
    border-color: {{ block.settings.secondary_button_border }};
  }

  .ai-split-hero-button-secondary-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover {
    background-color: {{ block.settings.secondary_button_hover_background }};
    color: {{ block.settings.secondary_button_hover_text }};
    border-color: {{ block.settings.secondary_button_hover_border }};
  }

  .ai-split-hero-caption-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.caption_font_size }}px;
    line-height: {{ block.settings.caption_line_height }};
    color: {{ block.settings.caption_color }};
    margin: {{ block.settings.caption_top_spacing }}px 0 {{ block.settings.caption_bottom_spacing }}px 0;
    max-width: {{ block.settings.caption_max_width }}px;
    {% if block.settings.button_alignment == 'center' %}
      text-align: center;
      margin-left: auto;
      margin-right: auto;
    {% endif %}
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ai-split-hero-caption-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      {% if block.settings.mobile_text_alignment == 'center' %}
        text-align: center;
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: auto;
      {% endif %}
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-trust-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: {{ block.settings.trust_item_gap }}px;
    row-gap: {{ block.settings.trust_row_gap }}px;
    margin-top: {{ block.settings.trust_top_spacing }}px;
    {% if block.settings.trust_alignment == 'center' %}
      justify-content: center;
    {% else %}
      justify-content: flex-start;
    {% endif %}
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ai-split-hero-trust-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      {% if block.settings.mobile_text_alignment == 'center' %}
        justify-content: center;
      {% endif %}
    }
  }

  .ai-split-hero-trust-item-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    font-size: {{ block.settings.trust_font_size }}px;
    color: {{ block.settings.trust_text_color }};
  }

  .ai-split-hero-trust-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    color: {{ block.settings.trust_checkmark_color }};
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .ai-split-hero-image-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    position: relative;
  }

  .ai-split-hero-image-wrapper-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: {{ block.settings.image_border_radius }}px;
    {% if block.settings.image_shadow %}
      box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    {% endif %}
    {% if block.settings.image_border %}
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
    {% endif %}
  }

  .ai-split-hero-image-panel-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    position: absolute;
    top: -20px;
    left: -20px;
    right: -20px;
    bottom: -20px;
    background-color: {{ block.settings.image_panel_background }};
    border-radius: {{ block.settings.image_border_radius | plus: 8 }}px;
    z-index: -1;
  }

  .ai-split-hero-image-wrapper-{{ ai_gen_id }} img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: block;
    {% if block.settings.image_aspect_ratio == 'natural' %}
      object-fit: {{ block.settings.image_fit }};
    {% elsif block.settings.image_aspect_ratio == '4-3' %}
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
      object-fit: {{ block.settings.image_fit }};
    {% elsif block.settings.image_aspect_ratio == '3-2' %}
      aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
      object-fit: {{ block.settings.image_fit }};
    {% elsif block.settings.image_aspect_ratio == '1-1' %}
      aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
      object-fit: {{ block.settings.image_fit }};
    {% elsif block.settings.image_aspect_ratio == 'portrait' %}
      aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
      object-fit: {{ block.settings.image_fit }};
    {% endif %}
  }

  .ai-split-hero-image-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 100%;
    background-color: #f4f4f4;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    {% if block.settings.image_aspect_ratio == 'natural' %}
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    {% elsif block.settings.image_aspect_ratio == '4-3' %}
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    {% elsif block.settings.image_aspect_ratio == '3-2' %}
      aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
    {% elsif block.settings.image_aspect_ratio == '1-1' %}
      aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    {% elsif block.settings.image_aspect_ratio == 'portrait' %}
      aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
    {% endif %}
  }

  .ai-split-hero-image-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }} svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    max-width: 300px;
    max-height: 300px;
    opacity: 0.3;
  }
{% endstyle %}

